From: ios-milanf-port (desk phase, 2026-10-25)
Subject: [PATCH] MILANF: hw.machine and hw.model have to be this device

The second and last negated board gate in the tree, found by teaching
`guards.py` to look for them after 0094 turned one up. A negated gate is not a
site that loses milanf code - it is a site that keeps Apple's arm, which on
this port is wrong in a way that is invisible in the log and visible to every
userspace process that calls `uname(2)`.

The gate:

    #if XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX && defined(__arm64__) && !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)

`XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX` is 1 for this build - `makedefs/MakeInc.def:72` adds it for
the macOS deployment target, which is what the port builds; that is also why
sweet's gate does anything at all. So milanf takes the `#if` arm:

    case HW_MACHINE:
        if (proc_platform(req->p) == PLATFORM_IOS) {
            strlcpy(dummy, "iPad8,6", sizeof(dummy));   /* hardcoded */
        } else {
            strlcpy(dummy, "arm64", ...);
        }
    case HW_MODEL:
        PEGetProductName(dummy, 64);   /* -> getMachineName() on arm64 */

and the `#else` arm - the one both boards want - is:

    case HW_MACHINE:  PEGetMachineName(dummy, 64);
    case HW_MODEL:    PEGetModelName(dummy, 64);

What those resolve to is not a guess. `SweetPlatformExpert` derives from
`IODTPlatformExpert`, and on arm64 the four callouts map like this:

| callout | reads | value on milanf |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `getMachineName` | provider `model` | `iPhone10,3` |
| `getModelName` | first `compatible` | `D22AP` |
| `getTargetName` | `getModelName` | `D22AP` |
| `getProductName` | `getMachineName` | `iPhone10,3` |

and `tools/mkadt-milanf.py:271-272` publishes exactly that: `compatible =
D22AP | iPhone10,3 | motorola,milanf | qcom,sm6375 | xiaomi,sweet | AppleARM`
with `model = iPhone10,3`. So the two arms disagree on both variables:

| sysctl | milanf today | intended |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `hw.machine` | `iPad8,6` (iOS process) or `arm64` | `iPhone10,3` |
| `hw.model` | `iPhone10,3` | `D22AP` |

`hw.machine = "iPad8,6"` is the bad one: an iPad 8,6 is an A12 tablet, and
anything in the iOS userland that branches on `uname(2)` - MobileGestalt
clients, idiom/asset pickers, launchd conditions - is being told the device is
something the DT, the platform expert and the framebuffer geometry all say it
is not. `hw.model` then reports `iPhone10,3` where the target/product
convention wants `D22AP`, which is the exact inconsistency the upstream
comments above the block complain about.

`hw.target` and `hw.product` were already correct on both boards, because both
arms call `PEGetTargetName`/`PEGetProductName` - which is why this would not
show up in a casual `sysctl` sweep, only in the two deprecated variables.

The stale comment also moves while the gate is being widened. It reads "SWEET:
the macOS config runs the iOS userland, which wants the device-tree names
(hw.machine iPhone10,3, hw.model D22AP)" and it currently sits *inside* the
`#if` - that is, inside the arm it argues against, where it is dead code on
both boards. It now sits at the top of the `#else` arm, reworded to name the
boards and to say what the values actually are.

Widening the negated gate needs a line continuation: the original condition is
already 83 columns and adding a third term puts it at 124.

Verified without a compiler: fresh ci-art3, 0086-0095 applied one at a time in
order, every one exit 0, every touched file CR=0, patch CR=0. Link unverified;
CI in the morning.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_mib.c b/bsd/kern/kern_mib.c
index ac1eba0..5f8f0a7 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_mib.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_mib.c
@@ -518,9 +518,8 @@ sysctl_hw_generic(__unused struct sysctl_oid *oidp, void *arg1,
 		 * Deprecated variables.  We still support these for
 		 * backwards compatibility purposes only.
 		 */
-#if XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX && defined(__arm64__) && !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
-	/* SWEET: the macOS config runs the iOS userland, which wants the
-	 * device-tree names (hw.machine iPhone10,3, hw.model D22AP). */
+#if XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX && defined(__arm64__) && !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) \
+    && !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 	/* The following two are kludged for backward
 	 * compatibility. Use hw.product/hw.target for something
 	 * consistent instead. */
@@ -553,6 +552,12 @@ sysctl_hw_generic(__unused struct sysctl_oid *oidp, void *arg1,
 		dummy[64] = 0;
 		return SYSCTL_OUT(req, dummy, strlen(dummy) + 1);
 #else
+	/*
+	 * The Qualcomm boards run the iOS userland under the macOS config,
+	 * which wants the device-tree names rather than the hardcoded
+	 * "iPad8,6"/"arm64": hw.machine iPhone10,3, hw.model D22AP, both read
+	 * out of the ADT root node by IODTPlatformExpert.
+	 */
 	case HW_MACHINE:
 		bzero(dummy, sizeof(dummy));
 		if (!PEGetMachineName(dummy, 64)) {
